Camps in Israel are places with special symbolic significance.
The first camp was Camp David, where the leaders of both sides (President Nasser and Premier Ben-Gurion) met to resolve the problem of Arab-Israeli conflict.
Nowadays, Camp David is used as a place for annual talks between Israeli Prime Ministers and Palestinian Chairman Abbas at which there can be signing of relevant agreements.
According to different sources and definitions, camps in Israel may vary:
1) – From those that include only Jews – Israeli Kibbutzim;
2) – Those camps which were founded by Palestinian citizens in order to protect them from being persecuted;
3) – From Zionist and settler movements.
